WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:05.959
Sometime later I received a letter from Biddy, saying that Joe would be coming to visit me

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:11.951
the next day. I must confess that I did not look forward to his visit with pleasure,

3
00:00:11.952 --> 00:00:16.293
even though I had so many ties to him. If I could have kept him away by

4
00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:23.936
paying money, I certainly would have done that. But I got up early the next day to

5
00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:30.603
make sure that the sitting room and the breakfast table were tidy. I soon heard Joe on

6
00:00:30.604 --> 00:00:35.841
the stairs. I knew it was Joe by the clumsy way he came upstairs, thanks to his

7
00:00:35.842 --> 00:00:37.753
dress boots, which were always too big for him. When the door was opened, he stood there,

8
00:00:37.754 --> 00:00:39.833
wiping his feet on the mat for what seemed like forever. "Joe, how are you?" "Pip, how

9
00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:44.920
are you?" With his good, honest face glowing, he laid his hat on the floor between us.

10
00:00:44.921 --> 00:00:50.753
He caught both my hands between his and worked them straight up and down as if I

11
00:00:50.754 --> 00:00:58.325
were a pump handle. He refused to let me take his hat, but set it on the

12
00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:04.666
narrow fireplace mantel. The hat immediately fell to the floor. Joe filled me in on all the

13
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:10.492
news from home: Biddy was as well as ever, and my sister was no worse. Mr. Wopsle

14
00:01:10.493 --> 00:01:15.888
had left his position as church clerk to become an actor and had accompanied Joe to London.

15
00:01:15.889 --> 00:01:20.968
Herbert joined us for breakfast. I felt impatient with Joe throughout the meal. Why had he dressed

16
00:01:20.969 --> 00:01:26.722
up in his best clothes when they made him so obviously uncomfortable? He sat far from the

17
00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:29.961
table and dropped more food than he ate and then pretended that he hadn't dropped it. I

18
00:01:29.962 --> 00:01:33.714
was glad when Herbert left for the counting house. "Now that we are alone, sir," Joe said.

19
00:01:33.715 --> 00:01:37.058
"Please don't call me sir ," I said peevishly. "Now that we're alone," Joe began again, "I

20
00:01:37.059 --> 00:01:45.384
will tell you why I'm here. The other night I was at the pub when Pumblechook came

21
00:01:45.385 --> 00:01:54.035
in. By the way, now that you're a gentleman, he often tells everyone that he was your

22
00:01:54.036 --> 00:01:55.702
companion when you were a child and that you looked upon him as a playmate." "Nonsense." "I

23
00:01:55.703 --> 00:02:00.789
know, Pip. Anyway he said Miss Havisham wished to speak to me." "Miss Havisham?" "Yes, so the

24
00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:02.273
next day, having cleaned myself up, I went to see her. She asked if I was in

25
00:02:02.274 --> 00:02:09.845
correspondence with you. And since we'd just had a letter from you, I said I was. She

26
00:02:09.846 --> 00:02:13.591
then asked if I would tell you that Estella has come home and would be glad to

27
00:02:13.592 --> 00:02:19.258
see you." I felt my face turn red as I looked at Joe. "And now that I

28
00:02:19.259 --> 00:02:22.266
have delivered her message," said Joe, "I must be going." "But you're coming back for dinner?" "No,

29
00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:27.170
I'm not. Pip, dear old chap, you and I are not meant to be seen together in

30
00:02:27.171 --> 00:02:29.258
London. I'm wrong in these clothes. I'm wrong out of the forge or off the marshes. You

31
00:02:29.259 --> 00:02:35.480
won't find half as much fault with me if you come to the forge when you want

32
00:02:35.481 --> 00:02:40.750
to see me. And so, God bless you, dear old Pip." He touched me gently on the

33
00:02:40.751 --> 00:02:48.909
forehead and went out. As soon as I'd wiped my tears, I hurried out and looked for

34
00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:52.051
him in the nearby streets, but he was gone. It was clear that I must go back

35
00:02:52.052 --> 00:02:58.139
home the next day, and at first it was equally clear that I must stay at Joe's. But

36
00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:04.893
after I had secured my place on the coach, and had been down to Mr. Pocket's and

37
00:03:04.894 --> 00:03:11.885
back, I was not so sure. I began to invent reasons for staying at the Blue Boar

38
00:03:11.886 --> 00:03:18.210
Inn. I would be an inconvenience at Joe's. I was not expected and my bed would not

39
00:03:18.211 --> 00:03:25.543
be ready. I would be too far from Miss Havisham's and she might not like that. I

40
00:03:25.544 --> 00:03:32.273
was taking the afternoon coach, and because it was now winter, I would not arrive at my

41
00:03:32.274 --> 00:03:37.353
destination until after dark. At that time coaches often carried convicts down to the docks for the

42
00:03:37.354 --> 00:03:44.020
prison ships. The convicts rode up behind the driver, and more than once I had seen them

43
00:03:44.021 --> 00:03:50.432
dangling their legs over the coach roof. So I was not surprised when Herbert, who had accompanied

44
00:03:50.433 --> 00:03:55.091
me, told me there were two convicts going on my coach. "There they are!" said Herbert, pointing

45
00:03:55.092 --> 00:04:01.845
to the convicts and their guard. The two convicts were handcuffed together and they had irons on

46
00:04:01.846 --> 00:04:09.084
their legs—irons of a style that I knew well. They wore gray clothing that I also knew.

47
00:04:09.085 --> 00:04:13.916
One of them was larger than the other, and I recognized him at once. He was the

48
00:04:13.917 --> 00:04:20.258
man who had stirred his drink with the file and given me two pounds! I knew he

49
00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:25.155
didn't recognize me because he looked right at me and went on talking and laughing with the

50
00:04:25.156 --> 00:04:31.909
other convict. At last it was time to go, and the only place for me to sit

51
00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:35.402
was on top of the coach. The convicts hauled themselves up as best they could, and the

52
00:04:35.403 --> 00:04:38.473
convict I'd recognized sat directly behind me. "Good-bye!" Herbert called out as we started forward. I thought

53
00:04:38.474 --> 00:04:41.823
it was fortunate that he had not called me Pip. I did not want the convict to

54
00:04:41.824 --> 00:04:49.545
recognize my name. It is impossible to express how acutely I felt the convict's breathing not only

55
00:04:49.546 --> 00:04:55.458
on the back of my neck but all along my spine. It made my skin crawl. The

56
00:04:55.459 --> 00:04:59.886
weather was miserably raw, and the convicts cursed the cold. I dozed off while considering how I

57
00:04:59.887 --> 00:05:03.633
might give the two pounds back to this man. When I woke up, it was dark and

58
00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:08.370
we were in the marsh country. The two convicts were now huddling together for warmth and leaning

59
00:05:08.371 --> 00:05:14.124
forward over me. The very first thing I heard as I awoke was the convicts discussing "two

60
00:05:14.125 --> 00:05:17.695
one-pound notes." "How did you get them?" asked the smaller of the two convicts. "He knew that

61
00:05:17.696 --> 00:05:22.187
I was going to be discharged from prison, so he slipped me the notes. He asked me

62
00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:27.529
to find the boy that had fed him and kept his secret and to give the boy

63
00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.846
the notes." "I'd have spent them. What happened to him?" "He was tried again for breaking out

64
00:05:29.847 --> 00:05:31.600
of prison and was made a prisoner for life." I would have jumped down from the coach

65
00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:35.910
to be left in darkness on the highway except that I knew the convict had no clue

66
00:05:35.911 --> 00:05:42.934
to my identity. I had grown up so much and was dressed so differently now; I no

67
00:05:42.935 --> 00:05:49.085
longer resembled the boy in the pub. Still, the coincidence of our being on the same coach

68
00:05:49.086 --> 00:05:54.410
was strange enough to fill me with dread. For this reason I resolved to get off the

69
00:05:54.411 --> 00:05:58.656
coach as soon as we reached town. I threw my little suitcase off the coach, got down

70
00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:06.802
after it, and was left at the first lamp on the first stones of the town pavement.

